From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <fardjad.davari2@jumbo.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add OpenRouter EU provider
X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: add EU OpenRouter provider with accurate cost accounting
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-provider
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none

Patch intent:
Add openrouter-eu with an EU endpoint, isolated credentials and caches,
autocomplete, TUI visibility, and pricing lookup that uses EU catalog and
endpoint cache rates.

Why it exists:
Routes EU OpenRouter traffic through eu.openrouter.ai while preserving separate
identity and credentials. Its distinct cache namespace must also be used for
pricing: otherwise Jcode cannot find the EU model rates and falls back to the
generic $15/M input and $60/M output estimates, substantially overstating EU
API-key spend. This includes BYOK inference, but is not limited to it.

Upstream integration points:
Provider core, runtime, isolated cache namespaces, pricing resolution,
catalog, selection, auth, session, CLI, autocomplete, and TUI.

Update guidance:
Preserve typed EU identity, separate credentials, isolated model and endpoint
caches, and EU-specific pricing lookup. Never use the standard OpenRouter cache
or generic fallback rates when a priced EU cache entry exists. Preserve /auth
parsing, model switching, and visibility.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-base openrouter_eu_pricing_uses_its_isolated_catalog_cache --lib
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-provider-openrouter-runtime eu_openrouter --lib
